WEBVTT

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.520
Look, the sky up above has begun to move.
Hora miageta sora ugokidashita yo

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.750
Your astonishment was so dazzling.
Odoroku kimi mabushikute

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.810
Should I forgive the lies you told me yesterday
Kinou tsuita uso mo yurusou kana

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.050
just because the morning light is so pretty?
Kesa no hikari kirei dakara

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:38.170
The sound of your laughter is always important to me
Kimi no warai goe itsu datte daiji da yo

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.820
because it gives me courage.
Yuuki kureru kara saa

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.680
It's not a lie.
Uso ja nai

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.460
It's a beauty really
It's a beauty really

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.610
Your voice whenever.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.990
It makes me have.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:51.660
Even the silliest things sound dear,
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:57.980
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo
Even the silliest things sound dear,

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.540
if it's your voice I hear.
kimi no koe nara

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.810
You're sad whenever.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.120
It takes you back.
You're sad whenever.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:05.460
It takes you back.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.840
My heart runneth over.
Hamidasu kokoro

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:16.040
Unable to control myself, I set off at a run.
Osaerarenakute hashiri dashita yo

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.050
I can forever.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.990
"Izumizaka Senior High School Seventh Year Entrance Exam"

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.790
SFX: *thump thump*

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.440
I'll go confirm the numbers for you.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.460
It must be great...

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.410
...to have a soccer scholarship and take it easy.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.010
I think Nishino was 168...

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:00.920
Komiyama, Manaka, and Toujou
were 171, 172, and 173.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.620
Let's see, Nishino is 168.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:10.930
Komiyama, 171... Manaka, 172... Toujou, 173...

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.430
Huh?

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.150
W-We failed.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.320
Manaka-kun, Komiyama-kun,
come here!

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.360
Your numbers are listed over here!

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:38.890
You will be contacted later
Waitlisted

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:44.350
W-We got in on the waiting list!!

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:48.130
I... <i>guess</i> you could call this "passing."

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.060
Maybe so.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.390
Do we really get to go to this school?

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.050
I'm sure we can, Komiyama!

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.500
Then, let us delve into the world of education again.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.070
Bah, Komiyama, I won't lose to you!

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:04.070
The Memorial Second Button

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.290
Congratulations to
all Graduates
56th
Graduation
Ceremony

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.580
Well, we did graduate today.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.420
Badge: Congratulations on Graduating

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.080
But I sure didn't expect to get into high school via waitlist.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.330
So, did you get the official acceptance notice?

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.070
It showed up yesterday.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.840
Isn't that great?

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.200
Yeah, but...

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.410
I still...

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.870
Haven't...

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:35.430
I-It's okay.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.790
You'll definitely get in too, Komiyama.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:45.260
I wonder if Toujou tested for Izumizaka instead of Oumi

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.640
because she wanted to make movies with me.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.960
Oh yeah! Once the graduation ceremony's over...

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:57.880
Hey. We're in the same school again.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.660
Manaka-kun?

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:05.330
Why did you pass up Oumi Academy for Izumizaka High School?

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.120
It was...

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.920
Will you tell me, Toujou?

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.250
N-No...

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.100
Don't you already know the answer to that question?

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.690
Meanie.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.260
Hey, Manaka-kun...

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.480
I know we're in high school now,

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.400
but could you give me some memories of our middle school days?

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.110
Memories?

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.390
Yes. That's because I like you, Manaka-kun.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.080
That's why I let you see my
strawberry panties on purpose.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.060
So, please.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.200
Even though I said memories of middle school, this will have to do.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:49.390
This will have to do.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.640
Gah! Just what am I imagining?!

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.650
On Board:

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.460
Abe Fujimoto.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.260
Yes!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.240
Himura Oichi.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:05.330
Yes!

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.030
Ever since exam day,

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:10.040
the only thing on my mind was Toujou.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.650
Just what happened?

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.850
I'm supposed to be
going out with Nishino...

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:19.660
Note: In Japan, guys commonly give their uniform's 2nd button to a girl at graduation as a symbol of their relationship or time spent together.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:22.990
Your second button is ours!

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:23.280
Wait up!

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.030
Let me down!

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:24.970
Note: In Japan, guys commonly give their uniform's 2nd button to a girl at graduation as a symbol of their relationship or time spent together.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.710
It must be nice to be a hit with the girls, like Oukusa.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.800
It's the 21st century and they're still
worried about second buttons.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:36.350
Yeah, well, it's a world that has nothing to do with us.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.350
Let's get out of here... Huh?

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:42.540
Komiyama, I have something I need to do.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:46.800
Oh, I see. You're treating me differently, now that you've passed?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.360
Fine! I'll go home alone!

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.630
My apologies, Komiyama.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:57.570
At least let me pray so that you're
accepted to Izumizaka.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:03.880
It's not like I made plans with anyone.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:08.880
I just don't feel like going home yet today.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.350
Aya-chan! Let me take
a picture with you!

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.200
Toujou, please read this letter!

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.820
Aya-chan, answer me!

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.680
They only just now realized Toujou's beauty.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:24.510
Toujou's not just a pretty face,
she's got a great personality!

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:30.240
But, it's not like I'm going out with Toujou.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.020
And now,

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:36.930
Toujou went and tested at Izumizaka for my sake.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.190
I really can't believe it.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.500
Junpei-kun!

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:47.240
Nishino.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.680
You're a mess.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:53.560
Oh this? I just got mobbed a bit,

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.560
so I got annoyed and ran away.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.870
What? Something wrong?

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.030
Your second button is mine.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.280
This represents the memories
of my middle school years.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.140
Memories...?

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.210
C'mon, we're going to the same school.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:28.000
I won't be a new student at Izumizaka.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.010
W-Why?

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:34.510
Junpei-kun, isn't there someone else you like, other than me?

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.490
Nishino, that is...

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:41.560
It didn't take much thinking to understand it.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.630
But it's okay,

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:48.550
I like Toujou-san too.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:52.770
And plus, Toujou-san
must like you back.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:00.690
So, which high school do you think I'm going to?

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.790
None other than Oumi Academy!

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.850
My parents told me to try it out.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:10.410
I didn't tell anyone I was taking the test, and I passed!

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.800
I wonder if this is because I studied with Toujou-san?

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:15.800
Just kidding.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:20.560
Anyway, I promised I'd do karaoke with some girls from my class.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:28.150
Nishino!

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.330
What?

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.700
Was there something you needed to talk to me about?

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.110
Erm, no... just...

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:43.110
I do have something to say.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:47.960
"Why did I choose Oumi Academy?"

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:52.230
I haven't really given up on you.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.300
That's why I'm going to Oumi Academy.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.250
Toujou-san's going to the same school as you

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:01.000
because she wants to make movies together, right?

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.940
But I don't have anything like that right now.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:09.560
That's why I was thinking I couldn't win, even if I went to the same school.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:13.070
That's why I'm going to go to Oumi Academy--

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.110
to find something for myself.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:16.570
Get it?

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.970
No, I don't get it. I mean,

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:24.590
I'm sure you've had a lot of cool boys confess to you.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.640
So why me...?

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:27.920
Yeah, really.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:35.010
But, your confession truly sparked something inside me.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.510
There's no logic when it comes to falling in love.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.750
That's for sure.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:47.440
Because logically, no one'd ever fall for me.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:52.300
My heart isn't so open that I'd
fall for someone I didn't like.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.940
It's okay, you have a lot of good characteristics.

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:02.520
Junpei-kun, congratulations on your waitlist-passing.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:04.320
I can take credit for that!

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:09.980
Bye!

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:25.960
I couldn't tell Nishino my feelings.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:30.400
In the end, I couldn't do anything but hurt her.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:38.760
You wouldn't want to lose this.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.560
Wow, what a beautiful sunset.

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:50.200
Today's the end of
middle school, isn't it?

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.950
After this, we'll be high school students.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:53.790
Yeah.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:58.510
Now that I think about it, this is our last chance to see this scenery.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:01.800
You're right. I liked this place.

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:03.380
You did, too?

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.830
You liked it too, right?

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:09.310
You're right, I liked it too.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.810
That's why I thought you'd be here.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:15.820
Thank you.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:27.590
N-No... The thread happened to break, and it happened to fall off!

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:29.720
It really was an accident.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:33.880
Who am I kidding?

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.270
Your second button?

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.880
It's nice that you can leave
memories behind for someone.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:43.890
I want something to remember, too.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.200
T-This is...

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:51.120
The same thing I
thought of this morning.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:56.510
Manaka-kun, I...

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.220
Hey!

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:01.640
You were way up here, Manaka?

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:05.650
Get a load of this!
I got into Izumizaka too!

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:08.000
I just now got the notice!

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:16.540
Aya-chan, I'm gonna be sticking
around another three years!

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.060
Yup!

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.670
This was how my last day of middle school...

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:25.240
...came to an end.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.240
W-Who the hell are you?!

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.420
Good morning, Junpei.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.850
This is <i>not</i> a "good morning"!
Who <i>are</i> you?

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:08.680
This is <i>my</i> room, you know!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.960
Who am l?

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.140
You really don't know?

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.560
Crybaby Junpei.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.570
Why? That lousy Hide-kun...

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:29.020
He took the game I bought,

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:31.680
and he won't give it back at all.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:34.130
Junpei, look!

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.250
I took the game back for you.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:39.830
Are you crying again?

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:42.980
You're a year older than me,
so don't cry.

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:45.760
You really are a crybaby, Junpei.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.850
Y-Yui?!

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:54.310
You finally remembered!

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:58.470
That's right, you used to live next door,

00:13:58.470 --> 00:13:59.810
but you moved away 5 years ago.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.950
You're that meddling girl who was a year younger than me!

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:07.090
Hey, I wasn't "meddling"!

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:09.740
Unless "meddling" means "always saving you"!

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.880
Why are you dressed like that?

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.120
Stop it, you dummy!

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:19.080
The Spring Storm
is a Childhood Friend

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.590
I'm so proud of you, Yui-chan.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:26.470
Checking out prospective high schools is a great use for spring break.

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:29.090
Yeah, Junpei should learn from your example.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:31.630
That really isn't anything special.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:33.820
I'm in my 3rd year of middle school anyway.

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:36.100
It's only natural to think about entrance exams.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.170
No no, it's still impressive.

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:39.310
Isn't it?

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:45.730
The place I moved to was deep in the
countryside, with a low population.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.580
And there aren't any
high schools nearby,

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:51.080
so everyone goes to the city and lives
in dorms while they're in high school.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:55.160
And I thought if I was going to do that, I may as well do it here.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:58.650
W-Wait just a second.
Are you saying that you're going to

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:00.760
live with us once you
get to high school?

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:04.900
No, I won't. There're schools with dorms around here.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.760
I already researched everything.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.300
I-Is that really true?

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:11.300
It is!

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:15.760
It's been five years, and you two
still get along as good as ever.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.510
Thanks for the meal.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:22.560
All right, Junpei, let's get going.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.730
G-Going?

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.450
To go visit high schools, of course.

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:30.020
That's why Yui-chan came all this way.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:34.240
That's right. Junpei, I'm
depending on your guidance!

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.170
The one and only Oumi Academy.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.130
I won't accept anything other than that.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:56.600
I never thought Yui's first choice would be Oumi Academy.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:00.160
Hey, did any of your classmates

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:02.820
get accepted to Oumi Academy?

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.830
If any did, I'd like to meet them.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.650
I've got questions for them, too.

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:14.200
I won't be a new student at Izumizaka.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:17.300
And you think I can ask Nishino such a thing?

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.830
What are you doing?

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:23.300
Well, theres no way an
unpopular idiot like Junpei

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.750
would have any
female friends like that.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.730
Y-You're wrong!

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.130
Even I...

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:30.610
Even you...?

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.760
No, erm...

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.050
Junpei?

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:38.140
I-It's nothing.

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:39.630
How strange.

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:45.780
What's wrong?

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.140
This is not good! Look at those eyes.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:55.070
Those dogs are planning to attack us.

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:57.200
I-It's okay.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:16:59.580
Yeah, they've got scary faces,

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.950
but you'll be fine if you don't make eye contact.

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.810
Don't provoke them!

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.670
They'll definitely attack us.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.720
Didn't something like this happen when we were little?

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:13.670
What did we do back then?

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:19.060
It was during our 3rd-grade year, when we were walking home from school...

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:23.590
That's right, you've hated dogs for a long time.

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:25.850
Snakes and spiders don't scare me.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:30.690
What do you suggest we do, stand still until they leave?

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:34.570
I don't wanna do that, stupid! Do something!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.540
You dummy! If you yell like that--

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.870
I know. Here.

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:49.780
Now! Run for it!

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:53.060
Aww, I was saving those meat buns for later!

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:54.300
This isn't the time for that!

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:56.550
Now I remember.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:00.140
Back then, you threw my baked fish at them,

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.010
and we ran away.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:06.020
Is that really something to dig up right now?

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:14.860
Sorry, it's actually a good memory.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:21.660
Because its a memory
of you saving me.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.660
As opposed to me always saving you.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.670
Hey, wait a second.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:30.420
Aren't you skewing these memories in your favor?

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:35.940
Huh? Suke and Kaku,
this is where you were?

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:39.680
Hey now, don't eat meat buns that someone dropped on the street.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:48.190
Man... Yui dragged me all over the place today.

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.180
Junpei!

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.570
I'm coming in~!

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:56.030
Why the sudden intrusion!?

00:18:56.350 --> 00:19:00.200
It's a reward for accompanying me to Oumi Academy.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.160
I'll wash your back for you.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:03.700
Hey...

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:07.190
You can't still be shy about
something like that, can you?

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.000
We used to bathe
together all the time.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.460
Come on, don't hold back.

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:20.750
This is kind of...

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:23.030
Even though she's like a little sister...

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:25.350
She's pretty quick to switch into "big sister" mode.

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.470
Did I miss anything?

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:32.480
No, that's more than good enough.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:34.690
Okay, next up's the shower.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:38.380
W-What are you doing?

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.700
I'm all wet.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.260
If you don't hurry up and change, you'll catch a cold.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:52.030
Okay.

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:57.800
Since I'm already wet, maybe I should just get in the bath too.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.850
Junpei, are you getting out already?

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.180
Whose fault is that?

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:11.690
She doesn't look at me as a guy, does she?

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.300
It feels good!

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:21.400
Yui, just how much longer do you plan on staying here?

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.700
Huh? I'm going home tomorrow.

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.630
It's an early morning train,

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:32.540
so I might already be gone when you wake up.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.470
I wonder if Yui got back safely.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:51.270
What the heck?

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:55.580
Good morning, Junpei. I overslept.

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.270
That's not the issue!
Why are you in here?

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.280
Because I overslept.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:06.320
Hey, Junpei. Do you think I'd make the train in time if I left now?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:07.980
How should I know?!

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:12.410
